From 191055b1d58c001e33d6164a2ed4cc092e4e0e03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:25:49 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] docs(guide): continuous 4-axis walkthrough on the Tormach
 770MX + microARC 4

"Your first continuous 4-axis program": a Rotary Parallel job on a round
bar, from the machine file and the work offset on the A centreline to the
posted program, read line by line (G93 on a move that turns A with X Y Z,
A counting on past 180, the A rate cap, G94 back), what the post refuses,
a run in the PathPilot simulator and a single-block air cut.

The page ends with an air cut and tells the reader not to cut: Rotary
Parallel finishes the model's end faces to the axis, which on a bar held
in a chuck is a cut through the bar (#2343). Rotary Offset is refused on
this machine file (#2344).

- examples/first-continuous-4axis-part.camproj, .nc and the model, built
  and held by crates/app/tests/continuous_4axis_part.rs (5 tests)
- three pictures drawn from the example by
  site/tools/first_continuous_4axis_pictures.py
- site/tests/test_first_continuous_4axis_part.py holds the page to the
  UI sources, the project, the program, the post and the pictures
- continuous-4-axis.md and the Multi-axis index no longer say that no
  post writes G93 or that tormach.cps indexes A only

Stacked on PR #2342 (#796).

Fixes #1904

